{title: From Greenland’s Icy Mountains}
{artist: Reginald Heber / Lowell Mason}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 509)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]From Greenland’s icy mountains,
[D]From [A7]India’s cor[D]al strand;__[A]__
[D]Where Afric’s sunny fountains
[D]Roll down [Bm]their [E7]golden [A]sand:
[D]From many an [A7]an[D]cient [G]ri[D]ver,
[D]From many a palmy plain,__[A]__
[D]They call us to deliver
[D]Their [Em]land from [A7]error’s [D]chain!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]What though the spicy breezes
[D]Blow [A7]soft o’er Ja[D]va’s isle;__[A]__
[D]Though every prospect pleases,
[D]And on[Bm]ly [E7]man is [A]vile:
[D]In vain with [A7]lav[D]ish [G]kind[D]ness
[D]The gifts of God are strown;__[A]__
[D]The heathen, in his blindness,
[D]Bows [Em]down to [A7]wood and [D]stone!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Can we, whose souls are lighted
[D]With [A7]wisdom from [D]on high,__[A]__
[D]Can we to men benighted
[D]The lamp [Bm]of [E7]life de[A]ny?
[D]Salvation! [A7]oh [D]sal[G]va[D]tion!
[D]The joyful sound proclaim,__[A]__
[D]Till earth’s remotest nation
[D]Has [Em]learned Mes[A7]siah’s [D]name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Waft, waft, ye winds, His story,
[D]And [A7]you, ye wa[D]ters, roll__[A]__
[D]Till, like a sea of glory,
[D]It spreads [Bm]from [E7]pole to [A]pole;
[D]Till o’er our [A7]ran[D]somed [G]na[D]ture
[D]The Lamb for sinners slain,__[A]__
[D]Redeemer, king, creator,
[D]In [Em]bliss re[A7]turns to [D]reign!
{end_of_verse}
